[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:85. Never Too Old to Learn]
[00:00.440] Passage 85 | 文章八十五
[00:02.790] Never too old to learn | 活到老学到老
[00:06.400] I have just received a letter from my old school, | 我刚刚收到母校的一封信，
[00:10.925] informing me that my former headmaster, | 信中告知我，我的老校长，
[00:14.010] Mr. Reginald Page, | 雷金纳德·佩奇先生，
[00:15.890] will be retiring next week. | 将于下周退休。
[00:18.665] Pupils of the school, old and new, | 全校学生，无论是老同学还是新同学，
[00:22.310] will be sending him a present to mark the occasion. | 都将给他送一份礼物以示纪念。
[00:26.215] All those who have contributed towards the gift | 所有为这份礼物捐款的人，
[00:29.985] will sign their names in a large album, | 都将在一本大纪念册上签名，
[00:33.105] which will be sent to the headmaster's home. | 这本纪念册将被送到校长家中。
[00:36.885] We shall all remember Mr. Page | 我们都将铭记佩奇先生，
[00:40.315] for his patience and understanding, | 感谢他的耐心和理解，
[00:43.100] and for the kindly encouragement he gave us | 以及他给我们的亲切鼓励，
[00:46.195] when we went so unwillingly to school. | 当我们不情愿地去上学时。
[00:50.380] A great many former pupils | 许多老校友
[00:53.415] will be attending a farewell dinner in his honour | 将于下周四
[00:56.515] next Thursday. | 参加为他举行的告别晚宴。
[00:58.865] It is a curious coincidence | 一个奇特的巧合是，
[01:01.940] that the day before his retirement, | 在他退休的前一天，
[01:04.265] Mr. Page will have been teaching | 佩奇先生教书
[01:06.617] for a total of forty years. | 已经整整四十年了。
[01:09.735] After he has retired, | 退休之后，
[01:12.290] he will devote himself to gardening. | 他将致力于园艺。
[01:15.095] For him, this will be an entirely new hobby. | 对他来说，这将是一个全新的爱好。
[01:19.575] But this does not matter. | 但这并不重要。
[01:21.995] For, as he has often remarked, | 因为，正如他常说的，
[01:24.915] one is never too old to learn. | 活到老学到老。